{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-161313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{[\\frac{(x-y)^{3}}{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z[x]_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{(1-y)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(0-y)^{3}}{3}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z(1-0)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{(1-y)^{3}+{y}^{3}}{3}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{(1-y)^{3}+{y}^{3}}{3}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{(1-y)^{3}+{y}^{3}}{3}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{(1-y)^{3}+{y}^{3}}{3}[z]_{z=0}^{z=2\\pi }+[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z]_{z=0}^{z=2\\pi })\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{(1-y)^{3}+{y}^{3}}{3}(2\\pi -0)+(-1+1))\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1-y)^{3}+{y}^{3}\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\pi }{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1-y)^{3}+{y}^{3}\\text{d}y & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}{[-\\frac{(1-y)^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}((-0+\\frac{1}{4})-(-\\frac{1}{4}+0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-161313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+1"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\pi +2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-39476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy+yz+xz\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-39476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy+yz+xz\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy+yz+xz\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(y+z)x+yz\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(y+z)\\,{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2}+yz[x]_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(y+z)(2-0)+yz(2-0)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}2(y+z)+2yz\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y$, treating $z$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}2(y+z)+2yz\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2(y+z)+2yz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2(1+z)y+2z\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}((1+z)[{y}^{2}]_{1}^{2}+2z[y]_{1}^{2})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}((1+z)(4-1)+2z(2-1))\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3(1+z)+2z)\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3+5z)\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3+5z)\\text{d}z & ={[3z+\\frac{5}{2}{z}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3(1-0)+\\frac{5}{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-39476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-39476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-39476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{17}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-39476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-82852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-82852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we apply the sum rule and write our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[0,1]\\times [0,2]\\times [-1,1]$ is a rectangular box, and each integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our sum of repeated integrals as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z\\,+\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate each of these separately:\n\n- For the first product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot (2-0)\\cdot (1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z & =(1-0)\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot (1-(-1)) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{16}{3}=\\frac{20}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-82852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-82852" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-82852" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\frac{17}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{20}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{22}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-82852" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{20}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{2}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z)]_{z=0}^{z=\\pi }\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+0))\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy\\,dx & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy]dx \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y]_{y=0}^{y=\\pi /2}\\,dx \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}(-0+1)\\,dx \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,dx & =-2{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-161299" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161299" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{14}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161299" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{14}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{z}({y}^{2}-x)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{z}({y}^{2}-x)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{z}{y}^{2}-{e}^{z}x\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{z}{[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=3}-x{e}^{z}[y]_{y=0}^{y=3}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{z}(9-0)-x{e}^{z}(3-0)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}9{e}^{z}-3x{e}^{z}\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}9{e}^{z}-3x{e}^{z}\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{z}(9-3x)\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(9-3x)[{e}^{z}]_{z=0}^{z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(9-3x)(2-1)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}9-3x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}9-3x\\,dx & ={[9x-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(18-6)-(9-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-161310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "9"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}z}\\frac{z}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}z}\\frac{z}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}z}\\frac{z}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{[z\\cdot \\frac{1}{z}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{z})]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{3}z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{z})]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{3}z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[\\frac{\\pi }{3}{\\int }_{0}^{y}dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi }{3}[z]_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot y\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,y\\,dy & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-161336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,dx]dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y+z)]_{x=0}^{x=y}\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+y+z)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0+y+z)\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+z)\\,dy\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $z$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+z)\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+z)\\,dy]dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y+z)]}_{y=0}^{y=z}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(z+z)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2z+z)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+z)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+z)\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2z-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3z-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2z-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3z-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,dz & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2z+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3z+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z]}_{z=0}^{z=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})]-[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0] \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}+0+0]-[-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-161330" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161330" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161330" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-40205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}{\\int }_{0}^{y+z}2xyz\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-40205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}{\\int }_{0}^{y+z}2xyz\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z}2xyz\\,dx]dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}[{x}^{2}yz]_{x=0}^{x=y+z}\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}(y+z)^{2}yz\\,dy\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $z$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}(y+z)^{2}yz\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dy]dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}z+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}{z}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=z}\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4}{z}^{5}+\\frac{2}{3}{z}^{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{5}\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{17}{12}{z}^{5}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{17}{12}{z}^{5}\\,dz & ={[\\frac{17}{72}{z}^{6}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{72}\\cdot 64 \\\\  & =\\frac{136}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-40205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-40205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-40205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{119}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{132}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{136}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{36}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{68}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-40205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{136}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{2}}\\frac{x}{z}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{z})\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{2}}\\frac{x}{z}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{z})\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{2}}\\frac{x}{z}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{z})\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{[\\frac{x}{z}\\cdot z\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{z})]}_{y=0}^{y={z}^{2}}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{z})]}_{y=0}^{y={z}^{2}}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡z-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z]_{z=0}^{z=\\pi /2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x(-0+1)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}x\\,dx & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{x=-1}^{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-161344" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161344" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161344" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-40497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}{\\int }_{0}^{x+z}72xyz\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-40497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}{\\int }_{0}^{x+z}(72xyz)\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}36xz[{\\int }_{0}^{x+z}2y\\,dy]dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}36xz[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=x+z}\\,dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}36xz(x+z)^{2}\\,dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}36{x}^{3}z+72{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+36x{z}^{3}\\,dx\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x,$ treating $z$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}36{x}^{3}z+72{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+36x{z}^{3}\\,dx\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}36{x}^{3}z+72{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+36x{z}^{3}\\,dx]dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[9{x}^{4}z+24{x}^{3}{z}^{2}+18{x}^{2}{z}^{3}]_{x=0}^{x=z}\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}51{z}^{5}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}51{z}^{5}\\,dz & ={[\\frac{17{z}^{6}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-40497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-40497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-40497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{11}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{13}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{17}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{23}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-40497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{17}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we apply the sum rule and write our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[0,4]\\times [1,2]\\times [0,1]$ is a rectangular box, and each integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our sum of repeated integrals as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}z\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate each of these separately:\n\n- For the first product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{4}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{4}{z}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(8-0)(\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{1}{3})(\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{7}{3})(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}z\\,\\text{d}z & =(4-0)\\cdot (2-1)\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{14}{3}-2=\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-161270" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161270" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161270" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{y}{z})\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we apply the sum rule and write our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{y}{z}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[0,\\pi ]\\times [0,2]\\times [1,e]$ is a rectangular box, and each integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our sum of repeated integrals as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\text{d}z+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{z}\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate each of these separately:\n\n- For the first product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\text{d}z & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi }\\cdot (2-0)\\cdot (e-1) \\\\  & =(1+1)\\cdot 2\\cdot (e-1) \\\\  & =4(e-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{z}\\,\\text{d}z & =(\\pi -0)\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot [\\operatorname{ln}⁡|z|]_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{y}{z})\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x=4(e-1)+2\\pi =2(2e+\\pi -2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-161308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4e+2\\pi -3"] ["math" "2(2e+\\pi -2)"] ["math" "2e-3\\pi +2"] ["math" "4(-e-2\\pi +3)"] ["math" "4e-\\pi +1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2(2e+\\pi -2)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{y}^{2}-4x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we apply the sum rule and write our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}4x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[0,1]\\times [1,2]\\times [2,5]$ is a rectangular box, and each integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our sum of repeated integrals as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{0}^{1}4x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate each of these separately:\n\n- For the first product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\text{d}z & =(1-0)\\cdot [{y}^{3}]_{1}^{2}\\cdot (5-2) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (8-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\text{d}z & =[2{x}^{2}]_{0}^{1}\\cdot (2-1)\\cdot (5-2) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{y}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z=21-6=15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-161307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "25"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{x}^{2}-4{y}^{3}-2z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we apply the sum rule and write our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[0,1]\\times [0,2]\\times [-1,1]$ is a rectangular box, and each integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our sum of repeated integrals as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}4{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{-1}^{1}2z\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate each of these separately:\n\n- For the first product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z & =[{x}^{3}]_{0}^{1}\\cdot (2-0)\\cdot (1-(-1)) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}4{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z & =(1-0)\\cdot [{y}^{4}]_{0}^{2}\\cdot (1-(-1)) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 16\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{-1}^{1}2z\\,\\text{d}z & =(1-0)\\cdot (2-0)\\cdot [{z}^{2}]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{x}^{2}-4{y}^{3}-2z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=4-32-0=-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-161271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-28"] ["math" "-32"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "22"] ["math" "36"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-28"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{2x{e}^{y}}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the domain of integration $R=[-1,2]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]\\times [-1,-\\frac{1}{2}]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{2x{e}^{y}}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}2x\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{y}\\,dy{\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}2x\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{y}\\,dy{\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,dz & =[{x}^{2}]_{-1}^{2}\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot {[-\\frac{1}{z}]}_{-1}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =(4-1)\\cdot (2-1)\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eef77488997008a875a191234550f1f791b3405bedab3db447a8a08557f2ba94"} {"question" "q-161268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "q-161268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d2a04781e25222ef5f6b11d2eb8bb6d7e6bd61769fc505cc098ae78fb208ce8"} {"question" "e-12389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{2} \\int_{-1}^{2} \\int_{0}^{1} x^2y+xz^2 \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/example-12389.json" "file_sha256" "cd50b270c8b1743a390486f35336b9dca79195d077b1405749724e421cb13ace"} {"question" "e-12389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}y+x{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}y+x{z}^{2}\\,dz]dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{[{x}^{2}yz+\\frac{x{z}^{3}}{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}y(1-0)+x(\\frac{1}{3}-0)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}x\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}x\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}x\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}y+\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{2}]}_{x=-1}^{x=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}y({2}^{3}-(-1)^{3})+\\frac{1}{6}({2}^{2}-(-1)^{2}))\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}3y+\\frac{1}{2}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}3y+\\frac{1}{2}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{y}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =(6+1)-(\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/example-12389.json" "file_sha256" "cd50b270c8b1743a390486f35336b9dca79195d077b1405749724e421cb13ace"} {"question" "e-12368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{0}^{x} \\int_{0}^{3-x-y} x \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/example-12368.json" "file_sha256" "c2dc2e245b0dfb480d9638ca20884c2fef90214ace5088e565112479ae222ba0"} {"question" "e-12368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{\\int }_{0}^{3-x-y}x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}[{\\int }_{0}^{3-x-y}x\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}x\\cdot [z]_{z=0}^{z=3-x-y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}x(3-x-y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x-{x}^{2}-xy\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x-{x}^{2}-xy\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x-{x}^{2}-xy\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[(3x-{x}^{2})y-\\frac{1}{2}x{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x-{x}^{2})(x-0)-\\frac{1}{2}x({x}^{2}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3}\\,dx & ={[{x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{8}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =8-6 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/example-12368.json" "file_sha256" "c2dc2e245b0dfb480d9638ca20884c2fef90214ace5088e565112479ae222ba0"} {"question" "e-12390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle  \\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\int_{1}^{4} \\dfrac{\\sin{y}}{x} \\: \\textrm{d}z \\: \\textrm{d}y \\: \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/example-12390.json" "file_sha256" "10356d36e9f06e4561e5a9c6aeb51c2ec857bf2044ea23d89e4b3653a6b82feb"} {"question" "e-12390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the domain of integration $R = [1,2] \\times \\left[0,\\pi/2\\right] \\times [1,4]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}{x}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{dx}{x}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy{\\int }_{1}^{4}dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy\\,{\\int }_{1}^{4}dz & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|]_{1}^{2}\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y]_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\cdot (4-1) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-0)\\cdot (0+1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\int_{1}^{4} \\dfrac{\\sin{y}}{x} \\: \\textrm{d}z \\: \\textrm{d}y \\: \\textrm{d}x = 3\\ln 2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060397/example-12390.json" "file_sha256" "10356d36e9f06e4561e5a9c6aeb51c2ec857bf2044ea23d89e4b3653a6b82feb"}] "usage" {"e-12368" [] "e-12389" [] "q-39476" [] "e-12390" []} "basis" 1928 "retractions" [[17592186198899 :question/problem "What is $∫_{0}^{1}∫_{1}^{2}∫_{0}^{2}xy + yz + xzdxdydz$?"] [17592186197963 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{2} \\int_{-1}^{2} \\int_{0}^{1} x^2y+xz^2 \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}y$."] [17592186197963 :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}∫_{0}^{1}x^{2}y + xz^{2}dzdxdy &= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}[∫_{0}^{1}x^{2}y + xz^{2}dz]dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}[x^{2}yz + \\frac{xz^{3}}{3}]_{z = 0}^{z = 1}dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}x^{2}y(1 - 0) + x(\\frac{1}{3} - 0)dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}x^{2}y + \\frac{1}{3}xdxdy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}x^{2}y + \\frac{1}{3}xdxdy &= ∫_{1}^{2}[∫_{-1}^{2}x^{2}y + \\frac{1}{3}xdx]dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}[\\frac{1}{3}x^{3}y + \\frac{1}{6}x^{2}]_{x =-1}^{x = 2}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}y(2^{3} - (-1)^{3}) + \\frac{1}{6}(2^{2} - (-1)^{2}))dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}3y + \\frac{1}{2}dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}3y + \\frac{1}{2}dx &= [\\frac{3y^{2}}{2} + \\frac{y}{2}]_{y = 1}^{y = 2} \\\\\n&= (6 + 1) - (\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186197955 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{0}^{x} \\int_{0}^{3-x-y} x \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}x$."] [17592186197955 :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}∫_{0}^{3 - x - y}xdzdydx &= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}[∫_{0}^{3 - x - y}xdz]dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}x \\cdot [z]_{z = 0}^{z = 3 - x - y}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}x(3 - x - y)dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}3x - x^{2} - xydydx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}3x - x^{2} - xydydx &= ∫_{0}^{2}[∫_{0}^{x}3x - x^{2} - xydy]dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}[(3x - x^{2})y - \\frac{1}{2}xy^{2}]_{y = 0}^{y = x}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}(3x - x^{2})(x - 0) - \\frac{1}{2}x(x^{2} - 0)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}3x^{2} - x^{3} - \\frac{1}{2}x^{3}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}3x^{2} - \\frac{3}{2}x^{3}dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}3x^{2} - \\frac{3}{2}x^{3}dx &= [x^{3} - \\frac{3}{8}x^{4}]_{x = 0}^{x = 2} \\\\\n&= 8 - 6 \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186197964 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\int_{1}^{4} \\dfrac{\\sin{y}}{x} \\: \\textrm{d}z \\: \\textrm{d}y \\: \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186197964 :question/worked-solution "Since the domain of integration\n\n$$\nR = [1,2] \\times \\left[0,\\pi/2\\right] \\times [1,4]\n$$\n\nis a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z)$, we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}∫_{0}^{π/2}∫_{1}^{4}\\frac{\\sin y}{x}dzdydx &= ∫_{1}^{2}\\frac{dx}{x}∫_{0}^{π/2}\\sin ydy∫_{1}^{4}dz\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}dx∫_{0}^{π/2}\\sin ydy∫_{1}^{4}dz &= [\\ln \\mid x \\mid ]_{1}^{2} \\cdot [- \\cos y]_{0}^{π/2} \\cdot (4 - 1) \\\\\n&= (\\ln 2 - \\ln 1) \\cdot (-\\cos (\\frac{π}{2}) + \\cos (0)) \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= (\\ln 2 - 0) \\cdot (0 + 1) \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= 3\\ln 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\int_{1}^{4} \\dfrac{\\sin{y}}{x} \\: \\textrm{d}z \\: \\textrm{d}y \\: \\textrm{d}x = 3\\ln 2\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186197630 17592186197631 17592186197632 17592186197633 17592186